698 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1608 0 R
/E (Michael has a background in cell biology, carrying out a PhD at the University of Dundee \(Scotland\) studying endocytic trafficking and lysosomal regulation. After a postdoctoral period at the University of Oslo \(Norway\) examining mitochondrial degradation, he joined AstraZeneca in 2018 as a part of the Advanced Drug Delivery department to research nanoparticle development.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
699 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1608 0 R
/E (At AstraZeneca he has combined an interest in microscopy with high-throughput assays, automation, and data visualisation to enable rapid formulation, development and characterisation of nanoparticle vectors from formulation to intracellular delivery, with a particular focus upon endosomal escape. He has been involved in combining multi-variate nanoparticle characterisation data with data modelling approaches to further understanding of in vitro to in vivo correlations, improving the utility of in vitro assays for nanoparticle development.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
700 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1608 0 R
/E (Recently he has switched to the Respiratory bioscience, working on current challenges in the respiratory space for diseases such as COPD and IPF whilst maintaining a strong interest in high-throughput imaging and automation solutions.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
