761 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1657 0 R
/E (Closing the loop: from single-cell perturbations to spatial interventions)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
762 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1659 0 R
/E (Abstract:)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
763 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1659 0 R
/E (Advances in single-cell and spatial omics now allow us to observe how biological systems respond to perturbations at unprecedented resolution. However, a central challenge remains: how to turn these measurements into a predictive and ultimately controllable understanding of complex biological systems.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
764 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1659 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
765 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1659 0 R
/E (By iteratively linking data, models, and experiments, this closed-loop perspective provides a foundation for systematically probing, understanding, and ultimately steering biological systems across scales.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
