/E (Jess joined EMBL-EBI as a Group Leader in June 2025. The focus of her lab is on using cell profiling to investigate the impact of environmental chemical exposures on human health. Prior to joining the EBI, she was a postdoc with Anne Carpenter and Shantanu Singh at the Broad Institute where she learned how to use machine learning \(including deep learning\) to extract biological insights from high-content imaging datasets. She earned a PhD in Bioinformatics from McGill University, where she worked with Niladri Basu and Jianguo Xia to develop web-based tools, algorithms, and databases for incorporating omics data into chemical risk assessments conducted by regulatory agencies around the world.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [5]
>>
