1205 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 412 0 R
/T (An ML-enabled HT framework for disease-relevant rare signaling events and synaptic dynamics)
/E (An ML-enabled HT framework for disease-relevant rare signaling events and synaptic dynamics)
/Pg 56 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1206 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 412 0 R
/E (Understanding disease-relevant neuronal phenotypes requires capturing dynamic processes across multiple spatial and temporal scales, from intracellular signaling to synaptic organization.  )
/Pg 56 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 412 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 56 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 412 0 R
/E (In all cases, machine learning strategies assist in segmentation and extraction of biologically interpretable features, unsupervised learning to identify heterogeneity and similarities across samples and supervised learning to establish disease signatures and identify hit compounds reducing disease phenotypes. )
/Pg 56 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 412 0 R
/E (Using this framework, we identified off target effects of clinically used drugs, identified common perturbations between pathogenic variants and variants of uncertain significance of SynGAP1 that could contribute to rare disease diagnoses, and identified candidate hit compounds for follow-up. In summary, the framework enables potentially actionable disease- and treatment-relevant insights.)
/Pg 56 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
