/P 421 0 R
/E (OME-Arrow is a data model and toolkit for working with bioimaging data in modern analytical environments. It unifies images, metadata, and derived measurements into a single structure organized as linked tables, enabling direct querying, filtering, and analysis using familiar operations in Python, R, and SQL. By making relationships between data explicit and queryable, OME-Arrow eliminates the need to manually reconstruct connections across files and tools.)
/Pg 65 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
